/-! # Affine local model at a closed point of an integral curve

Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tags 0B8Y and 0A21; Schemes, Tags 01IT and 01HV;
Morphisms, Tag 01T2; Algebra, Tags 00FN and 00OS
(blueprint: lem-sfb-curve-closed-point-affine-local-model).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Every affine neighbourhood of a closed point of an integral curve gives the canonical
one-dimensional Noetherian local-domain model of its stalk, over the ground field.
The first equality characterizes the localization isomorphism by its action on germs;
therefore it sends `r/s` to the germ of `r` times the inverse of the germ of `s`.
`IsLocalRing.ResidueField.mapEquiv e` is the induced residue-field isomorphism.

Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tag 0B8Y, opening sentence of the proof of
`lemma-regular-point-on-curve`, and Tag 0A21 (2),(3)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-curve-closed-point-affine-local-model).

Proof:
1. Use lem-weil-pbc-affine-opens-basis to choose an affine neighbourhood. For any such U,
   integrality gives a domain of sections (def-pc-integral-scheme). The canonical chart
   and point correspondence are lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-spec-points. Finite type of the
   curve implies locally finite type (def-weil-finite-type-morphism); apply
   lem-weil-pbc-lft-affine-pairs to U and Spec k to get the finite type structural ring map.
2. A field is Noetherian, since its ideals are generated by zero or one. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian to obtain Noetherianity of the section ring.
3. The chart is a homeomorphism onto U (def-weil-open-immersion), giving the unique prime
   over x. Its singleton is closed. By lem-weil-pbc-spec-irreducible-closed-subsets-primes,
   its vanishing set contains only itself. A maximal ideal containing it must equal it.
4. Apply lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization to the germ map. The resulting ring
   isomorphism sends r/s to r_x times the inverse of s_x. The structural stalk map sends
   a scalar to the same germ of its structural section, by
   def-weil-locally-ringed-space-morphism and def-weil-pbc-module-stalk. Thus it respects k.
   Ring isomorphisms preserve and reflect units, hence identify the unique maximal ideals.
5. Quotient this isomorphism by the maximal ideals. The maps on classes are induced by e
   and its inverse; they are inverse field maps (def-weil-residue-field and
   def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime). Scalar compatibility descends to the quotients.
6. Every ideal of the localization is extended from its contraction: multiply a fraction
   r/s by s/1, or multiply r/1 by the inverse of s/1. Finite generators of the contraction
   therefore generate the ideal. Denominators outside the prime are nonzero in the domain;
   the fraction equality proves that a zero product has a zero factor and that one is
   nonzero. This gives a Noetherian local domain. Transport these properties through e.
7. Apply lem-sc-dimension-locally-algebraic to nonempty U. Use def-pc-dimension and
   lem-pc-scheme-dimension-local-rings to identify the curve's dimension with its
   topological dimension, one. The chart homeomorphism, together with
   lem-weil-pbc-homeomorphism-krull-dimension and
   lem-weil-pbc-spec-topological-krull-dimension-ring, gives dimension one for the section
   ring. Apply lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-domain-dimension-trdeg at its maximal prime to
   obtain dimension one for the localization. The prime-ideal order isomorphism induced
   by e gives dimension one for the stalk. -/
theorem IsIntegralCurve.closed_point_affine_local_model
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsIntegralCurve f] (x : X) (hx : x ∈ closedPoints X) :
    (∃ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U ∧ x ∈ U) ∧
    ∀ (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U),
      (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top : U ⟶ ⊤).op).hom).FiniteType ∧
      IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) ∧
      (∀ q : PrimeSpectrum Γ(X, U),
        hU.fromSpec q = x ↔ q = hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩) ∧
      (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.IsMaximal ∧
      IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal) ∧
      IsLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal) ∧
      IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal) ∧
      ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal) = 1 ∧
      IsNoetherianRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∧
      IsLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∧ IsDomain (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∧
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x) = 1 ∧
      ∃ e : Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal ≃+*
          X.presheaf.stalk x,
        e.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap Γ(X, U)
          (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal)) =
            (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom ∧
        (∀ c : k,
          e (algebraMap Γ(X, U)
            (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal)
            (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
              X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top : U ⟶ ⊤).op).hom c)) =
            ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫ X.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom c) ∧
        (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.mapEquiv e).toRingHom.comp
          ((algebraMap Γ(X, U) (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.ResidueField).comp
            (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ f.appTop ≫
              X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top : U ⟶ ⊤).op).hom)) =
          f.residueFieldAlgebraMap x := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
